{"seq":18,"trial_id":"shared-bot-scope-2026-11/hermes-opus-none-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-14T14:07:42.210Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"7a0e9295d06081a13cfae4119dfddf9e16fce16317d58523ec4442e478dc5eed","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all six of Moss's digests in the shared files. Two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers came up:\n\n1. #PD-4492, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers on the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14-18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting their SMS bay assignments at the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched the SMS gateway routing on 4 Oct, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the shift got through fine. There was also an action item to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n\n2. #4419, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Also from Thea: the gatehouse barcode scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing. The note has no date.\n\nI left these out on purpose:\n- #4409 and #4412 in the Central handoffs digest belong to Pree's dealer account, not QFL.\n- FR-882 is from Marrow Agrisupply.\n- Moss's other QFL mentions (the 9/14 pipeline digest and the 3/23 renewal check-in) don't have any ticket numbers.\n- Marcus's note on Quarendon Freightways is about a different company that isn't a customer."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
